Question 20

A group of poets known as "Ashtadiggajas" adorned the kingdom of:

(a) Harihara
(b) Bukka
(c) Ala-ud-din Hassan
(d) Krishna Devaraya ✅

✅ Correct Answer: (d) Krishna Devaraya

Krishnadevaraya was one of the greatest rulers of the Vijayanagara Empire.

During his reign, eight famous Telugu poets were associated with his royal court. They were called:

Ashtadiggajas = "Eight great elephants" 🐘🐘🐘🐘🐘🐘🐘🐘

The name represents the eight pillars of Telugu literature.

🧠 SSC Shortcut

Ashtadiggajas → Krishna Devaraya → Vijayanagara Empire

